From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:23:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 76/78] test(discord): run launch-retry loops on a virtual
 clock (gcp-sq1r)

The `Run Python pack tests` CI step was OOM-killed at the runner pod's 4Gi
cgroup limit, surfacing as GitHub's "self-hosted runner lost communication"
annotation with no failing step (the kernel took Runner.Listener in the same
memcg sweep, so the agent stopped heartbeating and never uploaded the log).
Measured per-file, then per-test: one test accounted for the entire footprint.

`resolve_routable_session_candidate_eventually` polls until `time.monotonic()`
passes a 30s deadline, pacing itself with `time.sleep(0.25)`. Three tests
stubbed `common.time.sleep` with a bare `mock.patch.object`, which removes the
pacing but leaves the wall-clock deadline intact -- so the loop spun at full
speed for the whole 30 real seconds. Measured 43M iterations, and because the
stubs are MagicMocks every one of those calls is retained in `mock_calls` /
`call_args_list`. That recording, not the production code, is the allocation:
re-running the same loop with plain function stubs peaks at 32.7MB, with
MagicMock stubs at 5120MB.

Replacing the bare sleep stub with a `virtual_clock()` helper -- a fake
`monotonic` advanced by a plain-function `sleep` -- keeps the test's real
semantics (it still exhausts the full 30s retry budget, ~120 iterations at the
0.25s delay) while costing no wall time and no recorded calls. Applied to all
three sites, so the two hydration tests that currently self-bound by iteration
counter cannot regress into the same spin if those counters ever change. No
production change: with a real `sleep` the loop was always well behaved.

Validation, on the exact CI argument list from ci.yml line 44
(`python3 -m pytest tests contributing/tests gascity/tests discord/tests
github/tests slack-full/tests slack-channel/tests pr-pipeline/tests
gauntlet-tdd/tests -q`), max RSS via /usr/bin/time -l:

  before  5,422,563,328 B = 5.05 GiB   102.1s
  after     155,353,088 B =  148 MiB    55.9s

839 passed, 7 skipped, 9483 subtests in both runs -- same result set, so this
is a cost change only. 5.05 GiB against a 4Gi limit is the OOM; the observed
anon-rss of 3.87GiB was simply where the kernel caught it on the way up.

The suite's honest high-water mark is ~148 MiB, so 4Gi is ~27x headroom and
raising the runner pod's memory limit in bastion (half (A) on this bead --
modules/linux/helm/arc/runner-scale-set-hough-labs-values.yaml, already 221%
overcommitted at maxRunners=6) is NOT needed and should stay parked.
---
 discord/tests/test_discord_intake_common.py | 37 +++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/discord/tests/test_discord_intake_common.py b/discord/tests/test_discord_intake_common.py
index 40b02e0..d31ba68 100755
--- a/discord/tests/test_discord_intake_common.py
+++ b/discord/tests/test_discord_intake_common.py
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 from __future__ import annotations
 
+import contextlib
 import io
 import pathlib
 import socket
@@ -18,6 +19,36 @@ sys.path.insert(0, str(pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / "scripts"))
 import discord_intake_common as common
 
 
+@contextlib.contextmanager
+def virtual_clock():
+    """Run a deadline-bounded retry loop on virtual time instead of the wall clock.
+
+    ``resolve_routable_session_candidate_eventually`` (and its ready-state sibling)
+    poll until ``time.monotonic()`` passes a deadline, pacing themselves with
+    ``time.sleep``. Stubbing only ``sleep`` removes the pacing but keeps the
+    wall-clock deadline, so the loop spins at full speed for the entire real
+    timeout -- ~43M iterations over 30s, and ~5GiB of recorded calls if the stubs
+    are MagicMocks. That is what OOM-killed the CI runner at its 4Gi cgroup limit.
+
+    Advancing a fake ``monotonic`` from the stubbed ``sleep`` keeps the loop's
+    real semantics -- it still burns its whole retry budget, ~120 iterations at a
+    0.25s delay -- while costing no wall time and no memory. Sleeps advance by at
+    least a hair so a ``sleep(0)`` caller can never wedge the loop forever.
+    """
+    state = {"now": 0.0}
+
+    def fake_monotonic() -> float:
+        return state["now"]
+
+    def fake_sleep(seconds: float = 0.0) -> None:
+        state["now"] += max(float(seconds), 1e-6)
+
+    with mock.patch.object(common.time, "monotonic", new=fake_monotonic), mock.patch.object(
+        common.time, "sleep", new=fake_sleep
+    ):
+        yield
+
+
 class DiscordIntakeCommonTests(unittest.TestCase):
     def setUp(self) -> None:
         self.tempdir = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()
@@ -1029,7 +1060,7 @@ class DiscordIntakeCommonTests(unittest.TestCase):
             common,
             "deliver_session_message",
             return_value={"status": "accepted", "id": "gc-new"},
-        ), mock.patch.object(common.time, "sleep"):
+        ), virtual_clock():
             current = common.ensure_room_launch_session(launch)
 
         create_agent_session.assert_called_once()
@@ -1074,7 +1105,7 @@ class DiscordIntakeCommonTests(unittest.TestCase):
             common,
             "deliver_session_message",
             return_value={"status": "accepted", "id": "gc-maya"},
-        ), mock.patch.object(common.time, "sleep"):
+        ), virtual_clock():
             current = common.ensure_room_launch_session(launch)
 
         create_agent_session.assert_called_once()
@@ -1134,7 +1165,7 @@ class DiscordIntakeCommonTests(unittest.TestCase):
             common,
             "create_agent_session",
             return_value={"alias": "dc-123-sky"},
-        ), mock.patch.object(common.time, "sleep"):
+        ), virtual_clock():
             with self.assertRaisesRegex(common.GCAPIError, "created launch session is not routable yet"):
                 common.ensure_room_launch_session(launch)
 
